# EOS Product and UX

Apply when editing UI surfaces (components, pages, styles). Control Plane today is mostly CLI/kernel; these rules apply if/when those paths exist or when building canary/web targets.

## Canonical sources

- `docs/workflows/WEBSITE_QUALITY_MODEL.md` — 10 quality dimensions
- `.agents/skills/accessibility-auditor/SKILL.md`
- `.agents/skills/performance-auditor/SKILL.md`
- `.agents/skills/seo-auditor/SKILL.md`
- `.agents/skills/browser-qa/SKILL.md`
- `docs/architecture/adrs/ADR-0008-value-driven-ui-architecture-and-friction-reduction.md`

## Product first

- Name the job-to-be-done, audience, and conversion (or operator) goal before visual polish.
- Prefer `NO_BUILD` when the page does not reduce a real friction.
- Application over template: intentional type, spacing, and palette — not stock theme dumps.

## UX / UI

- Clear hierarchy, keyboard-usable flows, visible loading / error / empty states.
- Responsive checks at 375px, 768px, 1440px when layout changes.
- Verify behavior in the browser, not a single screenshot. Exercise the changed flow end to end.
- Shared state must stay consistent across routes that read it.

## Accessibility, performance, SEO

- Semantic HTML, focus indicators, contrast ≥ 4.5:1, ARIA only when needed (WCAG 2.1 AA).
- Core Web Vitals targets: LCP < 2.5s, INP < 200ms, CLS < 0.1 (measure; do not claim).
- Titles, meta description, canonical, OG tags, and no empty heading outline when the surface is public.

## Verification

A render screenshot is not verification. Click, type, submit, navigate. Hunt regressions on sibling routes. If browser tools are unavailable, say what was not verified and use tests/curl as substitute.
